Since $~$ is reflexive, $x in [x]$ for all $x in X$, so the classes cover $X$. It remains to show that for all $x, y in X$, either $[x] inter [y] = emptyset$ or $[x] = [y]$. Suppose $z in [x] inter [y]$; then $z ~ x$, so $x ~ z$ by symmetry, and $z ~ y$, so $x ~ y$ by transitivity. Now any $w in [y]$ satisfies $y ~ w$, hence $x ~ w$, so $w in [x]$ and $[y] subset.eq [x]$; by symmetry $[x] subset.eq [y]$. Therefore $[x] = [y]$, and the equivalence classes form a partition of $X$.
